00:02:25.060 --> 00:02:29.850
<i>What should we do?</i>
<i>We're not used to facing adversity</i>

00:02:29.850 --> 00:02:35.020
<i>So our resolve's definitely not all there</i>

00:02:35.020 --> 00:02:37.440
<i>Back then, we were just</i>

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:39.770
<i>Envious of others and</i>

00:02:39.770 --> 00:02:44.480
<i>Angry at something we couldn't see</i>

00:02:44.480 --> 00:02:47.020
<i>We just kept glaring at the next step</i>

00:02:47.020 --> 00:02:49.400
<i>That we could've easily taken</i>

00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:54.350
<i>And it was eating away at us silently</i>

00:02:55.770 --> 00:02:58.150
<i>We were so scared that we went numb</i>

00:02:58.150 --> 00:03:00.560
<i>And our legs buckled from under us</i>

00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:05.440
<i>We still can't forget the tears</i>
<i>that fell back then even now</i>

00:03:05.440 --> 00:03:10.230
<i>Even though we're so frail we might break,</i>
<i>we still continued to seek love</i>

00:03:10.230 --> 00:03:15.400
<i>We don't want to forget the reason</i>
<i>we're standing on this stage</i>

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:20.190
<i>Because you're the one who made me stronger</i>

00:03:20.190 --> 00:03:24.650
<i>I give you this lovely ballad</i>
<i>within this beautiful attack</i>

00:03:41.650 --> 00:03:44.690
What Mimura said earlier...

00:03:44.690 --> 00:03:50.020
I guess he was telling me
that I wasn't doing my job as the ace.

00:03:50.020 --> 00:03:53.480
It's my job to make sure you're doing your job.

00:03:53.480 --> 00:03:56.980
It's not like our win or loss
was all up to one player,

00:03:56.980 --> 00:04:02.560
but I ended up trying to put it all on you
out of spite, and this happened.

00:04:02.560 --> 00:04:03.340
I'm sorry.

00:04:03.340 --> 00:04:03.980
I was just--

00:04:03.980 --> 00:04:05.440
But...

00:04:05.440 --> 00:04:08.190
The reason for my spite was...

00:04:08.190 --> 00:04:12.310
...I wanted to show everyone
how amazing our ace is.

00:04:17.650 --> 00:04:19.560
Wait, your nose is still bleeding?

00:04:19.560 --> 00:04:24.200
No, it stopped! It stopped, but started
up again because you said that!

00:04:22.310 --> 00:04:24.690
What are you yelling for?

00:04:24.690 --> 00:04:26.810
I told you to rest!

00:04:26.810 --> 00:04:28.190
I-I'm sorry.

00:04:28.190 --> 00:04:30.020
Well, did it stop?

00:04:30.020 --> 00:04:34.350
It did! It stopped completely,
so please examine me again!

00:04:35.350 --> 00:04:37.520
What time does the fourth set start?

00:04:37.520 --> 00:04:38.940
I don't know.

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:41.730
Oda- <i>senpai</i> !

00:04:43.600 --> 00:04:45.020
Kuroba, Haijima.

00:04:45.020 --> 00:04:46.730
Senpai, did we make it in time?

00:04:46.730 --> 00:04:48.730
You did.

00:04:48.730 --> 00:04:49.600
Hup!

00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:53.400
Both schools have their cheer squad
performances before the fourth set,

00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:56.480
so I asked ours to stall a bit.

00:04:56.480 --> 00:05:00.190
More importantly, Haijima,
you haven't rested at all, have you?

00:05:00.190 --> 00:05:01.810
I'm fine.

00:05:01.810 --> 00:05:02.650
Kuroba.

00:05:02.650 --> 00:05:03.770
You ready to go out there?

00:05:03.770 --> 00:05:04.940
I am!

00:05:06.650 --> 00:05:07.730
You back?

00:05:07.730 --> 00:05:09.270
Yes.

00:05:09.270 --> 00:05:10.150
Kuroba!

00:05:10.150 --> 00:05:11.310
Oh, hey.

00:05:11.310 --> 00:05:12.770
You okay?

00:05:12.770 --> 00:05:15.650
I'm fine. Sorry to keep all of you waiting.

00:05:15.650 --> 00:05:17.730
I'm glad you made it in time.

00:05:17.730 --> 00:05:20.480
You're back, right? You've got this, right?

00:05:20.480 --> 00:05:21.980
Y-Yes...

00:05:21.980 --> 00:05:23.350
Oda- <i>senpai</i> ,

00:05:23.350 --> 00:05:27.810
I can put Kuroba in the lineup
for the fourth set, right?

00:05:27.810 --> 00:05:29.480
Oda- <i>senpai</i> , I'll sit out this game.

00:05:29.480 --> 00:05:31.850
No.

00:05:31.850 --> 00:05:34.350
Kuroba's coming back in my place.

00:05:34.350 --> 00:05:35.940
Is that all right?

00:05:48.650 --> 00:05:51.850
We're going to end Seiin's volleyball here.

00:05:55.190 --> 00:05:56.600
Hup!

00:05:58.150 --> 00:06:00.020
Haijima.

00:06:00.020 --> 00:06:01.100
Do that one thing.

00:06:01.100 --> 00:06:02.230
One thing?

00:06:02.230 --> 00:06:06.310
The thing where you push my back with your fist.

00:06:06.310 --> 00:06:07.770
Come on, put more into it!

00:06:07.770 --> 00:06:09.690
What do you even mean?

00:06:09.690 --> 00:06:11.810
You exhausted, or something?

00:06:11.810 --> 00:06:13.020
Ow!

00:06:13.020 --> 00:06:14.480
No.

00:06:15.850 --> 00:06:17.480
Hey.

00:06:17.480 --> 00:06:20.690
Is it normal to feel protected?

00:06:20.690 --> 00:06:23.350
Huh? By who?

00:06:25.820 --> 00:06:27.700
"Nanafu Seiin High School Boys Volleyball Team"
"Soar to the Nationals"

00:06:28.700 --> 00:06:35.580
"Nanafu Seiin High School Boys Volleyball Team"
"Soar to the Nationals"

00:06:32.020 --> 00:06:35.480
That's Gramps' calligraphy.

00:06:36.560 --> 00:06:38.650
Soar to the nationals...

00:06:40.690 --> 00:06:41.810
Let's win this.

00:06:42.040 --> 00:06:48.510
"Soar"

00:06:43.440 --> 00:06:48.400
We're gonna win and make
our way to the nationals.

00:06:49.510 --> 00:06:53.680
The 4th set

00:06:59.650 --> 00:07:00.770
Kuroba.

00:07:00.770 --> 00:07:04.310
When you hit up front, jump up
a bit further away from the net.

00:07:04.310 --> 00:07:05.850
Just where you think is right.

00:07:05.850 --> 00:07:07.100
I'll bring the ball to you.

00:07:07.100 --> 00:07:10.020
Huh? Are we coming up with a new attack?

00:07:10.020 --> 00:07:11.900
No.

00:07:11.900 --> 00:07:17.400
We were so close to that net so it was
hard to play against those high blocks.

00:07:17.400 --> 00:07:20.440
You can even be as far back like
you're attacking from the back.

00:07:20.440 --> 00:07:24.730
Even then, your spikes get through pretty high.

00:07:24.730 --> 00:07:26.980
Smash it into their court.

